    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> <strong>Negative Atmosphere: Emergency Room Prototype</strong> is a free, first-person, short medical horror experience that is an early rendition of the prequel we envisioned for <strong>Negative Atmosphere</strong>.\u00a0<i>W</i>hile no further updates are planned, it remains available as an archival piece.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">In this prototype, you control the S.P.I.D.E.R. (Surgical, Procedure, Intervention, Diagnostic, Emergency, Response) robot aboard the TRH Rusanov. You\u2019ll perform two distinct operations: an autopsy on a cadaver to gather evidence and a surgical procedure on a pineapple.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Guided by Medical Officer Samuel Edwards, you\u2019ll gain an understanding of the core systems that have been substantially expanded.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">This prototype is a snapshot of the early stages of <strong>Negative Atmosphere: Emergency Room</strong>'s development, offering a glimpse of the atmosphere and mechanics that have since been significantly expanded and refined.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> </p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> <strong>Negative Atmosphere: Emergency Room Prototype</strong> is a free, first-person, short medical horror experience that is an early rendition of the prequel we envisioned for <strong>Negative Atmosphere</strong>.\u00a0<i>W</i>hile no further updates are planned, it remains available as an archival piece.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">In this prototype, you control the S.P.I.D.E.R. (Surgical, Procedure, Intervention, Diagnostic, Emergency, Response) robot aboard the TRH Rusanov. You\u2019ll perform two distinct operations: an autopsy on a cadaver to gather evidence and a surgical procedure on a pineapple.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Guided by Medical Officer Samuel Edwards, you\u2019ll gain an understanding of the core systems that have been substantially expanded.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">This prototype is a snapshot of the early stages of <strong>Negative Atmosphere: Emergency Room</strong>'s development, offering a glimpse of the atmosphere and mechanics that have since been significantly expanded and refined.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"> </p>",
